      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>An acrostic poetic form of Birkat haMazon for the the pre-fast meal, or Seudah Mafseḳet, before the ninth of Av. In the manner of the poetic Birkat haMazon variants recorded in the Cairo Geniza. In reference to several of the acrostics found in Lamentations, the letters Pe and Ayin are reversed.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Note: “<j:divineName>The CAUSE</j:divineName>” is used to translate the Divine Name <j:divineName>YHVH</j:divineName>, based on the philosophical idea of <j:divineName>God</j:divineName> as <j:divineName>the Prime Mover</j:divineName> and on the interpretation of <j:divineName>the Name</j:divineName> as a causative form of the copula – “causes to be.”</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_33041_introduction"/>
